// 2026-11-26 (landing 177d2f, item 7, row 3: row C, form RABC5F, DEF-728; rulings l.31419 item 2). PRICES OFF PARITY, DEF-788 (LOW, fails closed,
// made by row C): a getter's view read through a pointer it loads from its parameter's pointee (`ND->:p = (<-o).nx ??! E5;`, then
// `string_bytes((<-p).s)`) is laid at the argument's own member (`nA.s`), so a write-capable pointer to the argument held beside the view
// (`ND->[1]:na = [@nA];`) refuses a right program whose direct spelling main accepts. It is DEF-750's face by another road. Three faces, one case
// each: AW7's `aw7_b_st_rm_ok`, `aw7_b_st_rmf_ok` and `aw7_b_st_rmtern_ok`. Way out: `getter_loaded_ptr_def788_wayout_m89_st_rm_ok_dir_ok.npk` (the
// read written at the caller), which runs 67 on main and on every build of the stack. In the form of main's prices files.
mod:getter_loaded_ptr_def788_prices;
error:E5;
